.TH R_MEMPOOL_REALLOC_ENTRY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
r_mempool_realloc_entry \- reallocate an entry to a different size
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cmempool.h>

void *r_mempool_realloc_entry(r_mempool *rmp, void *addr, size_t size);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Changes the size of an allocated entry. If the new size does not require
moving to a differently-sized underlying allocation, returns the original
pointer unchanged (no copy); this applies whether the entry is served by
one of the pool's own fixed-size tiers or by the dynamic/heap fallback
path. Otherwise, allocates a new entry sized for the request, copies
min(old_size, new_size) bytes, and frees the old entry.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
rmp   Ranged memory pool
addr  Existing entry to reallocate, or NULL to allocate new
size  New size in bytes (must be > 0 and <= largest_size)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns pointer to reallocated entry on success
Returns NULL on failure
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
If addr is NULL, equivalent to r_mempool_alloc_entry()
If the new size does not require a differently-sized allocation, returns
the original pointer unchanged (no copy)
Otherwise, allocates new, copies data, frees old
Copies min(old_user_size, new_user_size) bytes
Old entry is automatically freed if reallocation succeeds
Thread-safe if pool created with single_threaded=false
Returns NULL if size is 0 or > largest_size, WITHOUT touching addr: a
  non-NULL addr is neither freed nor moved when size itself is invalid,
  exactly as if the call had never been made
Will assert if addr is non-NULL and was not obtained from this
r_mempool (corruption/foreign-pointer detection, mirroring
r_mempool_free_entry())
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR r_mempool_alloc_entry (3),
.BR r_mempool_free_entry (3)
